From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: match SM8150 frame RC timestamp policy

Xiaomi's SM8150 VPU5 driver maps FRAME_RC_ENABLE to a second firmware
property, VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP, independently of the selected rate
control mode.  The upstream Venus encoder already carries the HFI property
ID and packetizer but never sends it.

Mirror that VPU5 ABI for IRIS1.  This matters at the first ETB, where the
firmware starts consuming input timestamps, and leaves other Venus versions
unchanged.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -855,6 +855,23 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst, bool enc_psc)
 	ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &rate_control);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Downstream keeps timestamp based rate control as a separate VPU5
+	 * property.  FRAME_RC_ENABLE maps directly to "disable RC timestamp";
+	 * without it firmware first observes the mismatch when consuming ETB.
+	 */
+	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core)) {
+		en.enable = ctr->rc_enable;
+		ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP;
+		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &en);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		dev_info(inst->core->dev,
+			 "venus-test15: encoder rc timestamp disable=%u\n",
+			 en.enable);
+	}
+
 	/* Downstream forces this on for every non-VBR rate-control mode. */
 	if (IS_IRIS1(inst->core) &&
 	    rate_control != HFI_RATE_CONTROL_VBR_VFR &&
